From 18dd74422862e75acf895b577f1772a742f10da9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:51:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ioctl: GEM_CLOSE and the V3D driver ioctls (Raspberry Pi 4)

DRM_IOCTL_GEM_CLOSE and Linux's V3D ioctls (SUBMIT_CL, WAIT_BO,
CREATE_BO, MMAP_BO, GET_PARAM, GET_BO_OFFSET, SUBMIT_CSD) become scheme
calls with the function number as metadata, like the other DRM ioctls.
The structs follow include/uapi/drm/v3d_drm.h; the BO handle arrays of
the submits travel inline after the fixed part. SUBMIT_CSD is
serialised by hand because its wire form has an alignment gap.

A V3D daemon (v3dd) serves them, so Mesa's v3d driver can talk to it
through libdrm.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
